// Perishing: food that keeps for so long once it is made, then spoils
// (VILLAGE.md decision 8, slice 8).
//
// Cut points:
// - full:     food that is perishable (`keepsFor` more than 0: meat, a
//             meal) spoils at a time set as it is made: made, it keeps
//             that long; cooked, a meal keeps its `mealKeepsFor` from then,
//             whatever it was made of. That time is all there is: nothing
//             steps it, and nothing changes until it comes. Then the food
//             is spoiled food, as heavy, where it was: no longer food, so
//             nobody eats it. Food that keeps (grain, turnips) never
//             spoils. Salting and smoking are left out.
// - reduced:  the same.
// - abstract: the same: it needs no agent.
// - frozen:   the same: meat in a larder nobody is near spoils all the
//             same.
// - perception: what spoils is seen to be gone, and spoiled food there,
//             as anything made or ended is: by whoever sees it then, or
//             looks later. When it will spoil is not seen.
// - stacks:   a stack spoils whole, at once. Put with a stack of its unit
//             and merged, the two spoil at their times averaged, each
//             weighed by its mass: fresh meat buys older meat time, and
//             old meat costs fresh meat some.
// - hunger:   spoiled food isn't food (hunger/eating.tri's #Food), and is
//             made of rot (things.tri): no method finds it to eat, eating
//             it isn't possible, and nobody values it as food.
// - cooking:  cooking makes a meal of raw food (cooking/): it keeps its
//             `mealKeepsFor` from then.
// - agency:   spoiled food an agent believes it holds is put down where it
//             stands (`spoiled_put_down`, a goal arising from what is
//             held: agency.tri's #Arising), so a meal carried past its time
//             doesn't fill a hand for good.
// - becoming: perishing is one use of what becomes something else when
//             its time comes (#Becoming). Where a thing lies may give it
//             another course (`within`): a hide rots, and in the tan
//             becomes leather (tanning/); its time starts over as it is
//             laid in or taken out.
// - code:     the perishing domain (src/domains_perishing.odin), for all
//             that becomes: it stamps what was made at the last boundary
//             with its time, and what was moved into the place of its
//             other course, or out of it, with its time there; its
//             horizon is the next thing whose time comes, its one wake
//             then.
//             effect_cook sets a meal's; spoiling is carved, as death's
//             remains are (src/act_actions.odin's `become`); a merge
//             averages (src/kinds_body_kind.odin).

package perishing

// What becomes something else when its time comes: how long it keeps once
// made (0: it keeps, and its time is set by something else, or never);
// when its time is (0: not yet known, or never), set as it is made, or by
// what starts it (cooking); what it becomes then, as heavy, where it is
// ("": nothing, it is gone); and what its end is recorded as.
//
// Where it lies may give it another course: `within` a kind of container
// (its type's name: a hide, in a tan pit, tanning/), it keeps
// `keepsWithin`, becomes its `becomesWithin`, and ends as its
// `endingWithin`. Its time starts over when it comes to lie there, and
// again when it is taken out: how far along it was is lost (a shortcut:
// nothing yet has two courses to the same end, sooner and later, where it
// should be kept). `liesWithin` is which course its time is of.
#Becoming: {
    @component(Becoming)
    keepsFor:      *0ms | time & >=0ms & <=100d     @field(content, saved, inspect)
    becomesAt:     *0ms | time & >=0ms & <=10000d   @field(saved, proposable, inspect)
    becomes:       *"spoiled_food" | text           @field(content, saved, inspect)
    ending:        *"spoiled" | text                @field(content, saved, inspect)
    within:        *"" | text                       @field(content, saved, inspect)
    keepsWithin:   *0ms | time & >=0ms & <=100d     @field(content, saved, inspect)
    becomesWithin: *"" | text                       @field(content, saved, inspect)
    endingWithin:  *"" | text                       @field(content, saved, inspect)
    liesWithin:    *false | bool                    @field(saved, proposable, inspect)
}

// What perishes: it keeps so long once made, then spoils: what it becomes
// is spoiled, or nothing (it rots away).
#Perishable: #Becoming & {}

// Food perishes; a meal made of it keeps so long from when it is cooked.
hunger.#Food: #Perishable & {
    mealKeepsFor: *2d | time & >=0ms & <=100d  @field(content, saved, inspect)
}

// Spoiled: what was food (or a carcass, hunting/), gone off. It isn't
// food, nor made of it (things.tri's "rot", no kind of food): eating takes
// something made of food (hunger/eating.tri), and nobody values it as food.
// It rots away to nothing in ten days, wherever it is.
#Spoiled: #Body & #Perishable & { keepsFor: 10d, becomes: "" }

spoiled_seen: #Seen & { kindOf: "#Spoiled" } @family(seen)
spoiled_look: #Look & { kindOf: "#Spoiled", look: "food.spoiled" } @family(looks)

// Its mass is what spoiled, carved from it.
spoiled_food: #Spoiled & { material: "rot", mass: 1g }

// Getting rid of what has spoiled.
#Riddance: #Frame & { rot: #Body }

// Spoiled food in hand (a meal carried about past its time): put down
// where the agent stands, before whatever it is doing, which a full hand
// would keep it from.
spoiled_put_down: #Goal & {
    title:  "put down what has spoiled"
    arises: { held: true, slot: "rot", of: #Spoiled }
    done: {
        find:  ["rot"]
        match: #Riddance & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, rot: #Spoiled & { place: #OnTile | #Inside } }
    }
    worth: [#Flat & { value: 70 }]
} @family(goals)

put_it_down: #Method & {
    title: "put it down"
    goal:  "spoiled_put_down"
    rank:  1
    pre:   { find: ["rot"], match: #Riddance & { me: #Agent & { id: $me }, rot: #Spoiled & { place: #Held & { by: $me } } } }
    steps: [#Do & { op: "put_down", object: "rot" }]
} @family(methods)
